Witch Hazel is an animated cartoon character in the Warner Bros.

11
00:43:27,000 --> 00:43:33,000
Looney Tunes and Merrie Melodies series of cartoons and TV shows.

12
00:47:24,000 --> 00:47:30,000
Witch Hazel is a fairy tale witch antagonist with green skin, a round
figure, bulbous facial features, and a single tooth.

13
00:51:21,000 --> 00:51:27,000
The name is a pun on the witch-hazel plant and folk remedies based on it.

14
00:55:18,000 --> 00:55:24,000
Created by Chuck Jones during the golden age of American animation, the character
was originally voiced by Bea Benaderet in 1954's Bewitched Bunny.

15
00:59:15,000 --> 00:59:21,000
Benaderet would later be replaced by June Foray, who voiced the character almost exclusively
beginning with 1956's Broom-Stick Bunny and concluding with 2002's Twick or Tweety.

16
01:03:12,000 --> 01:03:18,000
Tress MacNeille would briefly voice Witch Hazel from 1992 to 1994
for episodes of Tiny Toon Adventures and Animaniacs.

17
01:07:09,000 --> 01:07:15,000
After Foray's departure from the role, the character was voiced by Roz Ryan from 2011 to 2013
for The Looney Tunes Show (as Witch Lezah) and by Candi Milo from 2017 onward.

18
01:11:06,000 --> 01:11:12,000
The film explores themes of cartoon, compilation, package film.

19
01:15:03,000 --> 01:15:09,000
The tone is lighthearted.
